## Types of polymorphism
- 1. Compile-time polymorphism(Method Overloading)
-- > Having mutiple methods with same name in same class but different Parameter.
1 : M in compile time

public class Student {
	void Math()
	{
		System.out.println("Student is Doing math home work");
	}
	void Math(int a )
	{
		System.out.println(a + "in math method with one Parameter");
	}

}

public class Main {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Student s = new Student();
		s.Math();
		s.Math(23);
	}
}

Student is Doing math home work
23in math method with one Parameter


-2. Runtime Polymorphism(Method Overriding)
Note:- Runtime passing the adress is known is Run time polymorphism
-- > Having mutiple methods with same name in same class but different Parameter
- 1.m runtime

public class Developer {
	void work()
	{
		System.out.println("Developr is Wrking");
	}
	void project()
	{
		System.out.println("Developer doing Project");
	}
}

public class JavaDeveloper extends Developer
{
	void work() {
		System.out.println("JavaDevloper is working");
	}
	void project()
	{
		System.out.println("JavaDevloper is doing java Project");
	}
}


public class PythonDevloper  extends Developer
{	
	void work() 
	{
		System.out.println("PythonDevloper is doing python programming");
	}
	void project()
	{
		System.out.println("PythonDevloper is doing a Python Project");
	}
}
public class Main {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Developer dev = new JavaDeveloper();
		dev.work();
		dev.project();
		
		Developer dev1 = new PythonDevloper();
		dev1.work();
		dev1.project();	
	}
}
